  "title": "Erdős Problem #890",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "If $\\omega(n)$ counts the number of distinct prime factors of $n$, then is it true that, for every $k\\geq 1$, $ \\liminf_{n\\to \\infty}\\sum_{0\\leq i<k}\\omega(n+i)\\leq k+\\pi(k)? $ Is it true that $ \\limsup_{n\\to \\infty}\\left(\\sum_{0\\leq i<k}\\omega(n+i)\\right) \\frac{\\log\\log n}{\\log n}=1? $ ",
